mod:store_path_cast_written;
// Landing 177d2b6, row 5 (form A, rulings Addenda 36 to 45): a store through a pointer whose first hop is a cast, walked at the type as WRITTEN too.
// Row 3 (H1, with F1t) reads the store's root chain at the first hop's type under its casts, the pointer's own; main read it at the cast's own type
// (`path_indirection_base_type`, deleted by H1). A ref out of a callee this walk can't read (a function value, by any road to one, or a named callee
// whose own retype goes through one) carries no DEF-585 mark, so it points at the cast's pointee and is no target at the pointer's own type: the store
// landed on another binding, and a pointer kept into the written one read freed heap. Row 5 walks the chain at the cast's type as well. One site per
// face, each a fault on fdc1724 (236 at -O0 and -O2 on roads 0-2, 97 under the detector):
//   the twenty-two releases of row 3, each refused by main at this site: `r_fv1`, `r_fv2`, `r_fvg` (a function value in a local, in the holder's
//   initializer, from a getter), `u_ffld`, `u_ffldc`, `u_fparam`, `u_fpick`, `u_fter` (taken from a field, called through the field, handed as a
//   parameter, chosen by a `pick`, by a ternary), `w_idx`, `w_nest` (the hop an array element, a nested field), `c_nmx` (a named callee that calls a
//   function value), `c_sl` (the hop a slice element), `c_two` (two casts at the store, a concrete type between), `c_twoc` (the callee's retype through
//   a concrete type), `x_gen` (a generic callee that calls the function value it is handed), `c_held` (a function value held in a
//   struct field, called later), `c_recv` (the store a method of the cast receiver), `c_fvfv` (handed through a second function value),
//   `k_fva` (taken from an array of function values), `k_fvm` (returned by a method), `k_arrn`, `k_arrs` (the holder an element of an array of
//   structs of structs, of structs);
//   `r_fvl` and `c_ptl`, two of DEF-674's faces (a pointer local as the store's root, the cast at the store), F on main too: the walk at the cast's type
//   is new there. DEF-674 stays open with `t2_plain`, `t2_ptr` and `v_fvo` (rulings Addendum 43).
// HELD, refused by every build: `t2_sib`, `c_dst` and `c_dstf`, where row 3 lost a site main reports and row 5 brings it back (`t2_sib` kills the
// mutant that reads the hop nearest the root as written).
// Each cell's declarations carry its name as a suffix, and its `main` is `cell_main_<name>`. The controls, which run, are in
// tests/backend/programs/store_path_cast_written_ok.npk.
// `u_ffld`, `u_ffldc`, `c_held` and `c_dstf` name their function-typed field `fx`, apart from the cell's own `func:f`, which takes the suffix.
// PRICE: the cell marked PRICE below is a right program the landing refuses, failing closed, at parity: its twins are refused on every build.
error:E5;
